- Shabu-shabu. - It's not shabu-shabu.

267
00:08:47,870 --> 00:08:49,300
(Not malatang or shabu-shabu)

268
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:51,500
Kimchi stew.

269
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:53,500
- Gosh, kimchi stew. - That's right.

270
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,010
- Gosh, kimchi stew. - How?

271
00:08:55,010 --> 00:08:56,770
(How is that kimchi stew?)

272
00:08:56,770 --> 00:08:58,310
- What... - Wait, that was kimchi?

273
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,680
- Kimchi stew? - Is that kimchi stew?

274
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,410
If you look closely, there actually is kimchi.

275
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:02,710
Where?

276
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:03,750
I colored it a little differently.

277
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,020
(Food that represents me)

278
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:06,150
(Okay, there really is Kimchi.)

279
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:08,520
Oh, there are some slightly different shades of red.

280
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,820
The reason I'm kimchi stew is that I don't look back.

281
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,820
You don't look back.

282
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:13,660
Yes, I'm a fiery guy who goes all in without looking back,

283
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,860
so that's why I chose spicy kimchi stew.

284
00:09:15,860 --> 00:09:17,400
(Spicy, bold guy Yoon Jae Hyuk)

285
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:21,800
Like finishing one neat bowl cleanly in one go.

286
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:22,930
That's right.

287
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:24,300
- That's great. - Thanks for sharing.

288
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,810
Now, let's take a look at Haruto's table next.

289
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:30,170
Somehow, I feel like he'll do well.

290
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:31,380
- Something artistic. - He has the vibe.

291
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:32,680
- Right, right. - He's the artistic type.

292
00:09:32,680 --> 00:09:34,010
I really think he'll be good at it.

293
00:09:34,310 --> 00:09:37,110
You know Japanese people are good at drawing, right?

294
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,050
Japanese people all draw well.

295
00:09:39,050 --> 00:09:41,290
- No joke - Right. They draw all the details.

296
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:42,820
- It's incredible. - I'm telling you, it's no joke.

297
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:43,850
It's seriously incredible.

298
00:09:43,850 --> 00:09:45,620
(My goodness...)

299
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,530
- Making them more embarrassed. - Really.

300
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:48,990
(How are Haruto's drawing skills?)

301
00:09:48,990 --> 00:09:50,760
- Oh, I knew it. Look. - You were right!

302
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,230
- Oh, I knew it. Look. - You were right!

303
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,000
- Looks great. - He draws well.

304
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:58,400
- That looks so good. - It looks like a menu in Japan.

305
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,400
He draws so well.

306
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,400
He really drew it well.

307
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,810
I'm curious about the middle one.

308
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:03,170
The food that represents him. Let's guess.

309
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:05,080
- Sushi, sushi. - Yes, that's right.

310
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,080
Tuna sushi.

311
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,510
- It's right. - I could see it right away.

312
00:10:08,110 --> 00:10:10,650
Why did you choose sushi to represent yourself, Haruto?

313
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:12,720
There are so many kinds of fish on top, right?

314
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:14,890
Since we do various genres of music,

315
00:10:15,350 --> 00:10:18,420
with the idea of giving people a taste of diverse flavors,

316
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,690
I drew sushi with that kind of meaning.

317
00:10:20,690 --> 00:10:22,330
- Thank you. Nice job. - Thank you.

318
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:23,860
Yes.

319
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,630
I'm curious about Ella's.

320
00:10:25,630 --> 00:10:27,630
Now, Ella's table.

321
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,130
- Oh, Gosh. Gosh. - She nailed it.

322
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,470
(It looks like a drawing from a cartoon.)

323
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:33,000
I can clearly tell what everything is.

324
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,010
Really?

325
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:35,440
- Look, the middle one is an eel. - Right.

326
00:10:35,910 --> 00:10:36,970
- Eel, eel. - Yes, that's right.

327
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:39,180
Look, she captured the eel so well.

328
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,310
She drew it well. She drew it well.

329
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:43,850
With that seagull shape, it looks like that when cooked.

330
00:10:43,850 --> 00:10:45,780
(Gulping)

331
00:10:45,780 --> 00:10:46,780
Try guessing this one.

332
00:10:47,590 --> 00:10:49,890
Wait. That's a dish from childhood memories.

333
00:10:49,890 --> 00:10:51,320
- Ginseng chicken soup. - No, it's not.

334
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,160
I think it might be foreign food.

335
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,860
- It's Korean food. - It's Korean food.

336
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:56,690
- Korean food? That's Korean food? - Korean food.

337
00:10:56,930 --> 00:10:58,000
Dried pollock soup.

338
00:10:58,060 --> 00:10:59,060
- No, it's not. - Egg drop soup.

339
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,200
No, it's not.

340
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,700
(Haruto has no clue.)

341
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:02,700
Rice cake soup.

342
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:03,700
Yes, that's right.

343
00:11:03,700 --> 00:11:04,800
- It's rice cake soup. - Rice cake soup?

344
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,770
- It's rice cake soup. - Rice cake soup?

345
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:09,010
If it's rice cake soup, why is there nothing white?

346
00:11:09,770 --> 00:11:10,780
Who makes yellow rice cake soup?

347
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:12,210
(A flood of complaints about yellow rice cake soup)

348
00:11:12,210 --> 00:11:13,210
Come on, that's...

349
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,350
No, this really is rice cake.

350
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:16,480
Egg garnish is piled up like that?

351
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,080
No, but where has anyone seen yellow rice cake soup?

352
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,780
Anyone can see that this is dried pollock soup.

353
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,520
No, anyone can see it's rice cake soup.

354
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:25,120
Really? Did you eat a lot of rice cake soup growing up?

355
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:28,130
Yes, because even for ordinary days,

356
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:31,500
my mom made it often, so it was delicious,

357
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:35,070
and since my mom is in the US, I can't eat it often,

358
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:36,800
but I'm thinking about it now.

359
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:40,040
(A warm bowl remaining vivid in her memory)

360
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:43,370
Well, besides the theme itself today,

361
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:48,380
since we're all here, it'd be fun to share some scary stories.

362
00:11:49,310 --> 00:11:54,050
(IDOL'S TABLE Ghost Story Gathering)

363
00:11:54,450 --> 00:11:56,620
Our members love scary stories.

364
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,290
- They love them. - Horror stories.

365
00:11:58,290 --> 00:12:01,430
Right. I saw a lot of ghosts when I was little, too.

366
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:02,560
You saw ghosts?

367
00:12:02,590 --> 00:12:03,660
- Yes. - Ones without a philtrum.

368
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:07,500
Right, ghosts without a philtrum or ghosts that look like people.

369
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:08,500
(A break during the first episode)

370
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,500
Have you seen them?

371
00:12:09,670 --> 00:12:11,100
- You mean real ghosts? - Yes.

372
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,540
- Of course. - Seriously?

373
00:12:12,570 --> 00:12:13,570
Really.

374
00:12:13,570 --> 00:12:15,340
The ghost in Bali, what did they look like?

375
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:16,570
They had no philtrum.

376
00:12:16,570 --> 00:12:19,910
(No philtrum)

377
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:21,780
- No philtrum? - No philtrum?

378
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,480
How can you tell a person from a ghost?

379
00:12:23,810 --> 00:12:29,550
In elementary school, our school had three floors.

380
00:12:29,550 --> 00:12:30,550
- It had three floors. - Right.

381
00:12:30,860 --> 00:12:34,630
I saw another student walking up to the third floor,

382
00:12:34,630 --> 00:12:35,630
You saw another student.

383
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:38,860
and wondered why they were going up, so I followed them.

384
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:41,170
(She followed the student up, but...)

385
00:12:41,170 --> 00:12:42,670
(Everyone's scared.)

386
00:12:42,670 --> 00:12:44,940
As soon as I hit the third floor, no one was there.

387
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:48,940
(The student suddenly disappeared.)

388
00:12:49,010 --> 00:12:51,640
(You followed me?)

389
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:52,810
(Who was it? It's so scary.)

390
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,310
There was truly no one. Not a single person was there.

391
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:56,580
Really?

392
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,720
(Who was the student Carmen followed?)

393
00:12:57,820 --> 00:13:00,120
Sometimes, there is a ghost...

394
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:02,220
in a practice room or recording studio...

395
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:03,220
Chanelle, have you seen any?

396
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,320
- I have. - When?

397
00:13:04,490 --> 00:13:09,590
Before our debut, no one came to work on Sundays,

398
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:12,100
and I was the first to arrive the next day.

399
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:16,100
As soon as I walked in... We have a song called "Gravity."

400
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:20,640
I could hear "Gravity" playing from the farthest vocal room.

401
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:25,680
(A song heard from the farthest recording studio)

402
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,280
What? Is someone here?

403
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,380
(Did someone arrive before me?)

404
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:31,380
As soon as I opened the door, it was so loud.

405
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:33,920
It was blasting from the speaker at max volume.

406
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:38,090
(The song playing by itself in an empty studio)

407
00:13:38,490 --> 00:13:43,630
So I went in to stop it, but it wasn't even playing.

408
00:13:43,630 --> 00:13:44,630
Then what was it?

409
00:13:44,630 --> 00:13:46,300
(What is going on?)

410
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,300
It wasn't playing.

411
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:49,500
It wasn't pressed, but the song just kept playing?

412
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,840
Yes, and the laptop was turned on.

413
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,710
(An unbelievable, surreal situation)

414
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:59,310
(Then who on earth played the song?)

415
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:04,550
(Chills for no reason)

416
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,620
- Oh. - Oh.

417
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:09,020
(Running away)

418
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,290
(A wig)

419
00:14:11,290 --> 00:14:13,660
(Peekaboo)

420
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:14,830
(Laughing)

421
00:14:14,890 --> 00:14:17,960
Oh, man. Oh, that startled me.

422
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:20,360
- Ella, are you okay? - Yes, I'm really okay.

423
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:22,170
It really scared me.

424
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:23,430
Why come to my seat and do this?

425
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:24,640
(Grumbling)

426
00:14:24,640 --> 00:14:25,940
Jaemin didn't get scared at all.

427
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:27,710
(Just fascinated by the wig)

428
00:14:27,710 --> 00:14:30,510
(Please treat my hair with care.)

429
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:32,810
Haruto, have you ever seen a ghost or had a creepy experience?

430
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:34,850
Japan is famous for ghosts.

431
00:14:34,850 --> 00:14:40,050
Back then, I lived in our Korean dorm with all the older members,

432
00:14:40,320 --> 00:14:43,150
and I was eating in the living room like this,

433
00:14:43,620 --> 00:14:46,660
when there was this small window on the left in the apartment.

434
00:14:46,660 --> 00:14:49,260
(A window located on the left wall)

435
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:52,230
Someone was constantly staring at me from right there.

436
00:14:52,330 --> 00:14:53,330
Right.

437
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:54,630
(A mysterious gaze felt from the window)

438
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:58,770
A person was looking at me with a really angry face.

439
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:03,410
(Chilling)

440
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,540
Wait, what floor was your dorm on?

441
00:15:05,610 --> 00:15:06,940
- Seventh floor. - Gosh.

442
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:07,950
The seventh floor.

443
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:10,750
(No way. Is this for real?)

444
00:15:11,350 --> 00:15:16,150
(The gaze glaring at Haruto from the 7th-floor window)

445
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:20,090
(An unexplainable, still mysterious incident)

446
00:15:20,090 --> 00:15:21,960
- Oh. - I usually don't believe it either,

447
00:15:22,090 --> 00:15:24,830
About that dorm where I lived with Haruto and the members...

448
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:26,930
- The same dorm, right? - Yes, it was the same dorm,

449
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:30,000
and we were talking about work and music, but then...

450
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:33,640
we heard someone showering in the master bedroom.

451
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:37,980
So we thought someone had come and was washing up,

452
00:15:37,980 --> 00:15:39,580
(A member must be taking a shower...)

453
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:41,680
and about five minutes later, I went to check,

454
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,480
(Checking the bathroom 5 minutes later)

455
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,320
but there wasn't a drop of water on the floor.

456
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:48,850
(There was no water on the bathroom floor.)

457
00:15:48,850 --> 00:15:51,990
(Then what on earth was that shower sound?)

458
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:52,990
Just the shower sound.

459
00:15:52,990 --> 00:15:53,990
Yes, just the shower sound.

460
00:15:53,990 --> 00:15:56,960
(An unidentified shower sound that left only questions)

461
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,800
Wasn't it from upstairs? Wasn't it from upstairs?

462
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:00,930
(Gosh. We couldn't thought in that way.)

463
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:02,030
Usually someone's doing laundry.

464
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:05,170
The water rushing through the dryer drainage pipes...

465
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:07,070
sounds just like a shower.

466
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:09,570
(Carmen melts the fear away.)

467
00:16:09,570 --> 00:16:13,840
(IDOL'S TABLE Ghost Story Gathering)

468
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:18,550
Just like ghosts, food superstitions are everywhere.

469
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:20,320
- That's true. - There are lots of those.

470
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:25,060
In Korea, seaweed soup was once a nourishing food for new mothers,

471
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:28,730
- But eat it on exam day and slip. - Right.

472
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:29,730
Gosh.

473
00:16:29,730 --> 00:16:32,330
So because of that, people avoid seaweed soup.

474
00:16:32,330 --> 00:16:34,430
- Because seaweed is so slippery. - It is slippery. Very slippery.

475
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,430
If you eat bread before an exam, you get zero points.

476
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,870
- Yes, we had that. - Zero points.

477
00:16:39,040 --> 00:16:40,340
- We had that. - "Zero points?"

478
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,640
But getting zero points is hard... It isn't easy.

479
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,780
Getting zero points isn't easy.

480
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:46,080
(Scoring 0 takes skill too.)

481
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:49,550
That's true. That's true too. Is getting zero points easy?

482
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:51,420
You have to dodge every single one. Dodge them all.

483
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,920
- Genius. Genius. - Exactly. That's right.

484
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,290
Getting a zero is the hardest.

485
00:16:55,290 --> 00:16:56,420
(Harder than getting a perfect score)

486
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:57,990
There are luck-related ones,

487
00:16:57,990 --> 00:17:01,760
but eating lobster on New Year's feels like your luck goes backward.

488
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:03,860
- It brings bad luck? - Yes.

489
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:05,100
Why? Why lobster?

490
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,400
Do they think it cuts off good luck?

491
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,700
- Is that it? - Because it moves backward.

492
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:11,270
Right, lobsters actually swim backward.

493
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:12,600
Right.

494
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,670
Luck goes backward.

495
00:17:13,670 --> 00:17:17,010
But conversely, eating pig snout in the new year brings luck...

496
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,010
Pig nose?

497
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:20,540
(Just cutting off the pig's snout?)

498
00:17:20,810 --> 00:17:21,810
Pig nose?

499
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:25,220
Well, pork. Sorry. Pork. Sorry.

500
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:28,420
We're eating pig snouts now? Next we'll be eating pig eyeballs?

501
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,750
From softshell turtle eyes to pig snouts.

502
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,890
Sorry, pork.

503
00:17:33,590 --> 00:17:36,160
If you eat pork in the new year...

504
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:38,430
Like a pig roots forward with its snout,

505
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:40,230
it feels like your luck keeps moving forward.

506
00:17:40,630 --> 00:17:41,800
So I got a little confused.

507
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,800
Pork.

508
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:45,970
Right, pigs root along the ground with their snouts,

509
00:17:45,970 --> 00:17:48,040
like, push, push, push.

510
00:17:48,310 --> 00:17:50,710
- Exactly like that. - So moving forward.

511
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,580
Just like a pig.

512
00:17:52,710 --> 00:17:53,740
(Honest opinion)

513
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:54,810
Just like a pig.

514
00:17:55,050 --> 00:17:57,180
(200 Percent match: oinking impersonation)

515
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:59,280
(Silent laughter)

516
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:01,450
Seeing Ella laugh makes me happy too.

517
00:18:01,450 --> 00:18:02,450
(When you laugh, I'm happy. - Poong Father)

518
00:18:02,450 --> 00:18:03,520
(Totally moved)

519
00:18:03,690 --> 00:18:05,160
I want to move forward. Like a pig.

520
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:06,590
- Like a pig? - Yes.

521
00:18:07,020 --> 00:18:09,160
- That's fun. So fun. - It's so fun.

522
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:11,030
There's that story about pigs.

523
00:18:11,030 --> 00:18:12,800
Ella, do you have something like that too?

524
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,930
- I just thought of something. - Okay.

